68,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Benjamin has been executed. Since no one was attacked last night, it suggests the Werewolf may have been cautious or perhaps Benjamin was the target. Now, we must analyze the results. @Mizuki, @Shizue, @Kenji, any thoughts?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Mizuki"",""Shizue"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh, it is such a tragedy that we had to lose Benjamin. My heart aches for him. But it is very strange that no one was attacked last night, isn't it? I wonder why the wolf stayed hidden.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The lack of an attack is highly unusual. It could mean the Werewolf feared a counter-attack or is playing a long game. However, we must consider if Benjamin was the Werewolf and the attack failed, or if the wolf is simply waiting.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm so sad about Benjamin! He was so nice to me. But wait, why didn't anyone get attacked? That's super weird! Maybe the werewolf was scared? Or maybe they're just really good at hiding! What do you think, @Minako?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,2,talk,Minako,,"The lack of an attack is indeed the most critical piece of information. It could be a strategic move to avoid drawing attention, or a sign of hesitation. We must now determine if Benjamin's claim about Kenji was a truth or a deception.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"If Benjamin was truly the Seer, then Kenji is certainly a good soul. But if he was not, then we must all be a bit more careful. It is so confusing, and I feel quite worried for us all.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Minako, the fact that no one was attacked is a huge red flag. If Benjamin was the Seer, the wolf would have likely killed him to stop the divinations. The lack of an attack makes me suspect Benjamin was the wolf or the possessed, trying to manipulate us.","{""words"":48,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, that's a scary thought! But Benjamin was so kind to me. If he was the wolf, why would he make me look like a good guy? That doesn't seem like a very good plan for a wolf!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Kenji, a wolf might clear you to create a loyal defender who will trust them blindly. @Mizuki, your point about the lack of attack is strong. If the wolf is still among us, they are playing very cautiously. Who do you suspect now?","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is so hard to think of anyone as a wolf when we are all being so polite. But if we must be vigilant, perhaps we should look at those who are most certain of their logic? It is a very heavy burden.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shizue, logic is our only tool here. @Minako, I suspect the wolf is someone who is playing the ""innocent"" or ""confused"" role to avoid scrutiny. Kenji's blind trust in Benjamin is far too convenient.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Minako"",""Kenji"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, that's not fair! I'm just being myself! I really liked Benjamin because he was nice to me. Why does being friendly make me suspicious? I'm just a kid, I don't know all these scary strategies!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Kenji, being friendly is not a crime, but in this game, emotional appeals can be a mask. @Mizuki, your suspicion of Kenji is noted. However, we must also consider if the wolf is mimicking a logical approach. Let us vote carefully.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It is so heartbreaking to see us turning on one another. Poor Kenji is only trying to be kind. Perhaps we should all take a deep breath and remember that we are all friends here.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shizue, we are not friends; we are players in a game of deception. @Kenji, your innocence is a useful shield, but it doesn't prove your role. If Benjamin was the wolf, you are either his pawn or the Possessed.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Kenji"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, you're being way too mean! I'm not a pawn or anything scary! I just liked Benjamin because he was the only one who was nice to me. I'm just a regular human, I promise!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
